# Normalize all text files to LF in the repo and on checkout, regardless of a
# contributor's local core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows checkout
# with autocrlf=true silently rewrites every tracked file to CRLF, which then
# fights Prettier's "lf" default (endOfLine, unset here since lf is already
# the default) and makes `prettier --check` falsely flag the entire repo as
# unformatted after nothing but a `git checkout`/`git merge` — not an actual
# formatting regression, just a line-ending mismatch. Binary assets are
# excluded so git never tries to diff/convert them.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ttf binary
*.wasm binary
*.ico binary
